    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We only ended up with n=12 for this cohort. I know it's on the lower side for this kind of study, but the depth of the neuroimaging data is incredible. Given how competitive the Symposium is, do you think we should be upfront about the small n, or is there a way to frame the methodology so it doesn't look like a weakness to the reviewers?",
